===A1_S3_D2===
// triggers when we walk into the settlement and talk to chione
Narrator: The Viridi settlement is hidden amidst the forest, with small buildings that make up a lively hub.
Narrator: It’s certainly now as large as the community on your home island, but the appearance of so many people — Viridi — around, helps you relax.
Chione: Amaya, you’re back! #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Chione: Who are these people with you? #portrait:ChioneNormal
Amaya: I found them outside, after they passed through the southern ruins. #portrait:AmayaThink
Amaya: They claim that this Krakenfolk is from another island, so I’ll need to speak to Silas. Can you keep watch? #portrait:AmayaThink
Chione: Of course! Go ahead. #portrait:ChioneNormal
// amaya sprite walks away
Narrator: Once Amaya has made her leave, Chione introduces herself to break the ice. 
Narrator: She explains that the Forest Watchers have been on high alert lately due to the strange weather going around. 
Chione: The ancient records have never mentioned a storm prior to the Great Floods before, so we’re all keeping an eye out for creatures or people who might’ve been affected by the weather last night. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Narrator: You smile, agreeing with the sentiment. 
Noelle: It was pretty bad out there. I’m lucky to be in one piece… #portrait:NoelleBigSmile
Amelia: Earlier during our walk… You said you wanted to fix your boat, right? #portrait:AmeliaNeutral
Narrator: While your boat may not be enough to sail through the floods, you <i>did</i> want to fix it up in case it’d come in handy. 
Chione: So you need supplies? Well… you couldn’t have come at a better or worse time. #portrait:ChioneHm
Noelle: What do you mean? #portrait:NoelleUm
Chione: We <i>are</i> in the season of collecting wood and such, but everyone’s focusing their efforts on the Great Floods. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Narrator: Knowledge about the Great Floods from your homeland is quite vague, to say the least. 
Narrator: You are aware that it happens every 500 years, caused by an enormous creature. 
Narrator: And that when the flood comes, Dusk would pack their entire lives onto their ships, sailing through the rising waves for months before settling back on land. 
Noelle: I see… resources are probably being stocked up, aren’t they? #portrait:NoelleUm
Chione: That’s right. But even with the floods, our way of life prioritises nature. So we only take as much as we need. #portrait:ChioneNormal
Narrator: You suppose that either way, it’d be a good idea to establish an amicable relationship with the locals if you can. 
Narrator: Both to potentially join their flood plans, and to fix up your ship in case sailing off might be a better option.
Narrator: Noticing your shift in expression, Chione tries to lighten the mood.
Chione: You must be pretty tired from today, right? Why don’t you familiarize yourself with the area? I can ‘keep an eye’ on you even from afar. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
Noelle: Are you sure? #portrait:NoelleShocked
Chione: Of course! I’ll wave you over once things are arranged. #portrait:ChioneLaugh
